sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/db966bc45986743c3cde6d87ef6b567099bb3b7b/claim-sources/aristotle-biology/inputs/pa.txt#line=422,423>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <http://classics.mit.edu/Aristotle/parts_animals.html>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "Thus in such animals as produce but few at a birth, whether horned quadrupeds or those with solid hoofs, the mammae are placed in the region of the thighs, and are two in number, while in such as produce litters, or such as are polydactylous, the dugs are either numerous and placed laterally on the belly, as in swine and dogs".
